{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wdrtuwjwnipkv6tvyidmbrewsvtjg3zyu2oua5akoxtbgfowoljq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The library is fully translated and verified.\n\n## Surface enumeration (definition of done)\n\nThe C build (`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` → one shared lib from `src/lib.c`) exports **7** public symbols. `lib.h` only declares `modeselect`, but all 7 non-static functions are exported, and there are no namespace-renaming macros. The symbol diff is **empty**:\n\n```\napply_multiplier   classify_mode   convert_negative_overflow   convert_time_factor\nget_modified_time  hash_time_value modeselect\n```\n\n## Key fidelity decisions\n\n| C construct | Handling |\n|---|---|\n| `apply_multiplier` switch with **no `break`s** (cases 4→0) | Fall-through unrolled per arm; `default` → `0xDEAD`. Verified for level −3…8. |\n| `(int)double` out of range (`convert_time_factor`, `convert_negative_overflow`) | Rust `as` *saturates*, x86 `cvttsd2si` yields `0x80000000`. Wrote a `d2i` helper reproducing the hardware \"integer indefinite\" result for overflow/NaN/±inf. |\n| `offset_days * 86400 + offset_hours * 3600` (signed `int` overflow, then widened to `time_t`) | `wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_add` in `i32`, *then* sign-extend. |\n| `time(NULL) >> 29` | Arithmetic shift, real libc `time()`. |\n| `hash_time_value` byte loop, `b << 24` and `hash *= 31` overflow | Computed in `u32` wrapping (bit-identical through the final `& 0x7FFFFFFF`). |\n| `modes[mode_selector % 4]` with negative selector (**OOB read**) | Reproduced via `read_volatile` on an offset stack pointer — C and Rust both exit 139 for −1/−2/−3/−5 and both succeed for −4/−8/`INT_MIN`. |\n| All `printf` formatting (`%.2e`, `%X`, `%ld`) | Calls libc `printf` directly, so formatting *and* stdout buffering/interleaving are identical rather than re-implemented. |\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release` clean; `libtranslation.so` exports all 7 symbols, diff vs C empty.\n- Differential harness (220,650 lines: all string cases, 96 `apply_multiplier` pairs, 22 doubles incl. ±inf, 289 `get_modified_time` pairs, 14 `hash_time_value` values, **22,022 `modeselect` calls**) — **0 diff lines**.\n- Randomized fuzz (20,000 iterations, 280,000 lines, random bit-pattern doubles incl. NaN) — **byte-identical** (`cmp` clean).\n- Matched against C built at `-O0`, `-O1`, `-O2`, `-Os`, `gcc -O3 -fwrapv`, and `clang -O0/-O2/-O3`: all zero-diff.\n\n## One thing worth flagging\n\n`gcc-11.5 -O3` specifically (i.e. `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release`) **miscompiles `hash_time_value`** by exploiting the signed-overflow UB in `hash *= 0x1F`: it constant-folds the first three loop iterations to `0x7FFFFFFF`, so the low 3 bytes of `t` stop affecting the hash and the result depends only on `t`'s top bytes (e.g. `htv(0) == htv(3) == htv(255) == 0x7E4B2761`).\n\nI translated the **source semantics**, which is what every other configuration produces — `-O0`, `-O1`, `-O2`, `-Os`, `-O3 -fwrapv`, and clang at every level. Only that one gcc `-O3` artifact differs, and matching it would have meant hard-coding a compiler bug that a plain `cmake && make` (no build type ⇒ `-O0`) or a plain `gcc -shared -fPIC` would not reproduce."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":449,"cache_read_input_tokens":70695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":449,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b078edac-6ca8-46bd-a36a-c183f46dddc5","uuid":"b648e7e0-a173-4a77-872f-3ed5fe603f7b","timestamp":"2026-08-28T04:18:01.380Z"}
